+## Customer evidence rules (lib/energy/customers.ts)
+
+- One record per conversation, **anonymised**: segment, region (Bundesland/country), size band, cost band, budget-owner **role**, stage. Never a name, person, email or organisation on the public site. Names live in the private CRM; the record cites its `ref`.
+- The funnel and the `qualified` / `pilots` KPIs are **derived** from records. Never type an "actual" anywhere.
+- Stages that count: `conversation`, `cost-named`, `data-shared`, `paid-trial`. `contacted` and `declined` do not. Compliments never do.
+- Every energy intake (form on `/`, `/energy/wedge`, `/energy/customers`) goes to the webhook with `cluster=energy`; the call it produces becomes a record the same day.
+- Wedge A kill condition (docs/energy/wedge-a/OFFER.md): ten conversations without one `cost-named` → new decision, wedge killed.
+
 ## Visualization rules (components/viz, lib/viz.ts)
 
 - Charts are **server-rendered SVG**, no client JavaScript. They read the same constants as the tables; a chart never carries a number the table does not.
